<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brisbane</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brisbane is the capital of Queensland, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, on the Brisbane River near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moreton-bay">Moreton Bay</a>. It began in 1825 as a penal settlement for convicts who had reoffended in New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-wales">South Wales</a>, moved from Redcliffe, and was opened to free settlers in 1842. It became the capital of the new colony of Queensland in 1859 and is now Australia's third-largest city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brisbane.jpg" alt="Brisbane" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chris Olszewski · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brisbane_CBD_seen_from_Kangaroo_Point,_2024,_01_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
